#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282021 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3332b534-bd04-5e86-995e-1e6d691d8e1b" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring and Using the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3cac7e64-8856-530f-ad04-b8f05d0976b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282023} {:answer/id #uuid "3aacf20c-49eb-5d97-85d7-02c5809de07b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282024} {:answer/id #uuid "fa5358f0-529c-5291-9deb-29fcfaa25bba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282025} {:answer/id #uuid "dfceceb6-5e5e-5d74-88bd-20f864435641" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282026} {:answer/id #uuid "ba7f0883-e6f7-57dd-8666-2d5285a24a61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282027}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dfceceb6-5e5e-5d74-88bd-20f864435641" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282026} :answer-field/id #uuid "0013e078-0457-53a9-b74e-da21aab11759" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282022}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cf848531-47fc-5901-8c19-787e41fbe811" :question/math-academy-id "q-119362" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression ${cos}^{3}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{5}⁡\\theta .$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the expression:\n\n$$\n{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{5}⁡\\theta ={cos}^{3}⁡\\theta ({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )\n$$\n\nThen, we use ${sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta =1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta ({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta ) & ={cos}^{3}⁡\\theta \\cdot 1 \\\\  & ={cos}^{3}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{cos}^{3}⁡\\theta {sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{5}⁡\\theta ={cos}^{3}⁡\\theta .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282028 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "868125f0-22e0-57fc-9620-f3242419a689" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Rational Expression Using the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "23693061-4348-5d12-a872-c23dd1b690ce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+{sec}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282030} {:answer/id #uuid "de9126ab-85a6-5a6f-ba7f-3f2654294de7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+{sec}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282031} {:answer/id #uuid "fcba337b-e599-54bc-957d-e517d1186379" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+\\operatorname{csc}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282032} {:answer/id #uuid "c7b87ff3-cbe6-56c5-b5ec-508ac0357f04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+{csc}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282033} {:answer/id #uuid "3136784e-60b1-58b5-88ba-359b1dcb9502" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tan}⁡x+\\operatorname{csc}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282034}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c7b87ff3-cbe6-56c5-b5ec-508ac0357f04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+{csc}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282033} :answer-field/id #uuid "8abbcd1c-0e5c-5939-af7e-9da6d799dd37" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282029}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "69124476-7712-5455-bad9-c2749d724009" :question/math-academy-id "q-119392" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{sin}^{3}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{3}⁡x+1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ from the first two terms of the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{sin}^{3}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{3}⁡x+1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}=\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)+1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\n$$\n\nNext, we use the Pythagorean identity to rewrite the expression in the parentheses, and then we simplify the resulting expression as much as possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)+1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot 1+1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}+\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}+{(\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+{csc}^{2}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{sin}^{3}⁡x+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x{cos}^{3}⁡x+1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}=\\operatorname{cot}⁡x+{csc}^{2}⁡x.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282035 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1bc8c875-3393-5fd6-90cf-87737e16f2f2" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Trigonometric Expression Using a Common Denominator and the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c310b27-dfc2-5fc4-b6bc-510f2bf63428" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282037} {:answer/id #uuid "84c29454-e450-5588-a5da-23b2c746ad69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282038} {:answer/id #uuid "46e0998c-4411-5790-99c7-390156555771" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282039} {:answer/id #uuid "e4e05a9b-91bb-5d49-b6fb-6f758c4bbd8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282040} {:answer/id #uuid "4d5dc51b-19f3-56d0-b6fc-8cabfae1688a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282041}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "84c29454-e450-5588-a5da-23b2c746ad69" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282038} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfb7cacd-4023-5e4c-8544-379376522bdd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282036}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "53417fe7-aa74-52f7-8a7b-cac1bef3c1c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-119767" :question/problem "$\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }=$" :question/worked-solution "We put both terms over a common denominator, and combine the two fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }+\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify using the Pythagorean identity, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta } \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }{\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta }=\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\theta \\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta .\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282042 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1bc8c875-3393-5fd6-90cf-87737e16f2f2" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying a Trigonometric Expression Using a Common Denominator and the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "52143fd5-aec2-550d-b233-1326538720a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282044} {:answer/id #uuid "3bb41a19-b67b-5816-8a1f-237944556101" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282045} {:answer/id #uuid "2e56a16a-c924-57f6-a992-86c7ae04efc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282046} {:answer/id #uuid "a5156e51-cf96-5115-bf53-1b03c3e49c58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282047} {:answer/id #uuid "4648cdf0-aa80-5732-810e-74e872d47f58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282048}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4648cdf0-aa80-5732-810e-74e872d47f58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282048} :answer-field/id #uuid "81390f49-093c-5b1b-92c3-af824077e155" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282043}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b1b11d95-94b5-51a5-999a-88076d2426a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-119775" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}.$" :question/worked-solution "We put both terms over a common denominator, and combine the two fractions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{1}-\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}-\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-{cos}^{2}⁡x}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify using the Pythagorean identity, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-{cos}^{2}⁡x}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x-{cos}^{2}⁡x}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-({sin}^{2}⁡x+{cos}^{2}⁡x)}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-1}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =\\frac{-(1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡x}{1-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}=-1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186282049 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3332b534-bd04-5e86-995e-1e6d691d8e1b" :knowledge-point/title "Simplifying an Expression by Factoring and Using the Pythagorean Identity"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ecd9792-80bd-5c8c-b380-07d0ec5c37cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282051} {:answer/id #uuid "76cf6920-79ff-5cb3-b415-abc8a0c24f39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282052} {:answer/id #uuid "e8cdfdbd-0405-5943-b759-acd289efe3d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282053} {:answer/id #uuid "24b43494-04fe-5204-85b9-6b200873e89d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282054} {:answer/id #uuid "1c2935c6-419b-566a-845f-0be6a3148ba6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282055}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76cf6920-79ff-5cb3-b415-abc8a0c24f39" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282052} :answer-field/id #uuid "08095a5c-9175-554f-8336-4d159562c7e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282050}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b09d2ae6-b1b6-58ca-ab31-441a63f5a985" :question/math-academy-id "q-65229" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta .$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ from the expression:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot ({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta )\n$$\n\nThen, we use ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot ({sin}^{2}⁡\\theta +{cos}^{2}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{3}⁡\\theta =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .\n$$"}]}
